IMPORT prelude

-- Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932 (Tas), Part VII (representative proceedings) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. Part VII counts "before the date so fixed" (s 71(2)), "not earlier than 6 months
-- after the day on which the order is made" (s 87(3)(c)), "on or before" a day (s 87(3)(c)) and "a further 21-day
-- period" (s 89(3)).
--
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (CC BY 4.0, State of Tasmania). For the
-- latest information on Tasmanian Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au. Unofficial copy; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for Part VII of the Supreme Court Civil Procedure Act 1932`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day (a negative number counts back).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The day before a day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day before` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS 1)

-- The number of days in a calendar month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The day n calendar months after a day: the same day-number n months later; where that month is shorter, its last day
-- (31 August + 6 months is 28 or 29 February). The day itself is excluded (the Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tas), a
-- borrowed rule, not deposited). Fork F9 in NOTES.md.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the month index` MEANS `the count` MODULO 12
        `the year` MEANS (`the count` MINUS `the month index`) DIVIDED BY 12
        `the month` MEANS `the month index` PLUS 1
        `the day number` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`
            THEN `the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`
